        "problem": "If $T={r,s,t},$ then $P(T)=$",
        "worked_solution": "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $\u2205.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $T$ using a tree diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14098182/assets/916d0207e217da90b6421244f0f02d59d8f9dbafc2a7045033eab5ae2b69740e.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $T$ are\n\n$$\n\u2205={},\\,{r},\\,{s},\\,{t},\\,{r,s},\\,{r,t},\\,{s,t},\\,{r,s,t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(T)={\u2205,{r},{s},{t},{r,s},{r,t},{s,t},{r,s,t}}.\n$$",
